# Terraform Module Standards (GCP)

## File Organization
- `main.tf` — provider requirements + data sources
- `{resource}.tf` — core resources, named by GCP resource type (e.g., `storage_bucket.tf`, `cloud_run_service.tf`)
- `locals.tf` — label construction, label merging, computed values
- `variables.tf` — module-specific variables
- `{{COMMON_VARS_FILE}}` — standard cross-module variables
- `outputs.tf` — module outputs
- `versions.tf` — terraform and provider version constraints

## Resource Conventions
- All single resources use identifier `"{{RESOURCE_IDENTIFIER}}"` (e.g., `google_storage_bucket.default`)
- Map-driven resources use `for_each` with descriptive keys
- Use `count` for boolean on/off features
- Labels: `{{TAG_MERGE_PATTERN}}` — always (GCP uses `labels`, not `tags`)

## Standard Variables (GCP)
- `prefix` — resource name prefix
- `project` — GCP project ID
- `region` — GCP region (e.g., `us-central1`)
- `labels` — additional labels (`map(string)`)
- `env_default_labels` — default labels from orchestration layer
- `network` — VPC network name (where applicable)
- `subnetwork` — subnetwork name (where applicable)

## Region vs Location
GCP resources use either `region` or `location` depending on the resource type:
- **`region`** — compute resources (Cloud SQL, Cloud Run, GKE, Memorystore)
- **`location`** — storage/multi-region resources (GCS buckets, Artifact Registry)
- **`zone`** — single-zone compute resources (Compute Engine instances)
Check the provider documentation for each resource type.

